      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just for extra explictiness of the code, I would add one initial step to check that `mtu \u003e 0`.\n\nAlso what happens when `mtu \u003d\u003d 0`. On ChromeOS the codebase tends to interpret mtu 0 values as meaning the default 1500 value. Is there any such convention on Android ?\n\nWe could add a companion function `resetInterfaceMtu(String ifname)` or `setInterfaceDefaultMtu(String ifname) that calls `setInterfaceMtu()` with `mtu \u003d\u003d 1500`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 508,
        "startChar": 73,
        "endLine": 508,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "aec2e717_886a2321",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
